{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/12732-covers-and-demonic-form","id":12732,"title":"Covers and Demonic Form","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-17T07:59:00-08:00","id":12732,"title":"Covers and Demonic Form","content":"When in Demonic Form - correct me if I'm wrong - you're not using any of your Covers, yes?<br /> <br /> For example, you can't get a Compromise for acting &quot;out of character&quot; when you're not &quot;in character&quot; in the first place.<br /> <br /> So ... how does that work? What happens if you fail a Compromise roll while in Demonic Form?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Nothing, because you don't have a Cover and can't lose it?<br /> <br /> The same as when in Cover, but the effects &quot;reset&quot; when you go back into hiding?<br /> <br /> Any Cover loss and Conditions are applied to the Cover you transform into when you leave Demonic Form?<br /> <br /> Any Cover loss and Conditions are applied to the Cover of your choice?<br /> <br /> Something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T08:07:08-08:00","id":12738,"title":"","content":"This is under the Extispicy Exploit:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Killing an animal (or a person, for that matter)</i><br /> <i>to read its entrails might constitute a separate compromise if doing so would be grossly out of character</i><br /> <i>for the demon\u2019s Cover. As such, some demons prefer to assume demonic form before gutting the</i><br /> <i>sacrificial creature (the claws often make it easier anyway).</i> </div> </div> </div>That leads me to think that since there is no such thing as being out of character when you're wearing your Demonic form, you can't roll for compromise, or at least not for that.<br /> Use of Exploits, abuse of certain Embeds, betraying facts about yourself, etc, however, are all fair game, since it's a matter of directly attracting the GM's attention.<br /> I'd say it applies to the Cover you last used before going Demonic. It doesn't seem to be directly stated in the rules, though. If you're stuck in Demonic Form and don't have any Cover left to which you could apply that, it's okay, because being stuck in Demonic form is its own punishment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":519,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","user":"ChairKicker","date":". 11-17-2013, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T08:10:12-08:00","id":12740,"title":"","content":"ChairKicker I'm pretty sure you are right there that compromise rolls are applied to the last used cover (it is implied a few times in the book).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T09:07:16-08:00","id":12760,"title":"","content":"There's no entry on the modifier table for Cover values and compromise rolls for Cover 0... I'm wondering if you just don't roll it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T09:12:26-08:00","id":12763,"title":"","content":"(Sorry about the double post, it won't let me edit.) Alternatively, use the -3 (like when shedding Cover to put Form on) but only apply the Conditions, not the loss of a Cover dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T21:59:33-08:00","id":13181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/12732-covers-and-demonic-form?p=12760#post12760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no entry on the modifier table for Cover values and compromise rolls for Cover 0... I'm wondering if you just don't roll it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Modifiers for cover values? You mean high / low cover?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T05:18:06-08:00","id":13337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/12732-covers-and-demonic-form?p=13181#post13181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Modifiers for cover values? You mean high / low cover?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the dice bonus or penalty you get on the Compromise roll for having a high or low Cover score, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T09:17:48-08:00","id":13431,"title":"","content":"If you're in Demon Form and you need to make a compromise roll, I'd say use the modifier associated with the Cover you most recently wore. After all, if you have a Cover of 0, that means that you've burned that Cover. And that means you'd better have another Cover handy, because if you burned your last Cover, you're already operating under at least two conditions.<br /> <br /> Also, I think I'd rule that if you had to make compromise roll and you didn't have any Covers left, it'd be an automatic failure. After all, if you're making a compromise roll in Demon Form, you're doing something that would attract the God-Machine's attention (as was said by ChairKicker), and since you don't have a Cover that can deflect suspicion or take the bullet, it's all on you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T09:36:56-08:00","id":13444,"title":"","content":"Hang on, so you make compromise checks while in Demonic Form which may drop the rating of your cover?<br /> <br /> Surely if your not in your cover you can't compromise it? I mean being in Demonic Form is basically waving a bit &quot;I'M OVER HERE&quot; flag anyway. So I don't see why any further compromise rolls (which would represent maybe getting the God Machines attention) would be necessary, with the exception of using Exploits as they seem to draw even more attention. <br /> <br /> Still I can't quite reconcile the idea that you can damage your Cover while not actually being in that cover. Can someone explain that thought process to me?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T09:50:03-08:00","id":13452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/12732-covers-and-demonic-form?p=13444#post13444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wisdom</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with Hawthorn. I don't quite remember whether I saw it, but I seem to remember something about demons shedding their cover briefly into demonic form so that they could do terrible horrible things and not have their cover suffer for it.<br /> <br /> I am interested in how this works as well.<br /> <br /> EDIT - Found it, it's under the Extispicy Exploit:<br /> <br /> &quot;Extispicy works on any living creature of Size 4 or greater. <b>Killing an animal (or a person, for that matter) to read its entrails might constitute a separate compromise if doing so would be grossly out of character for the demon\u2019s Cover. As such, some demons prefer to assume demonic form before gutting the sacrificial creature</b> (the claws often make it easier anyway).&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":323,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/323-hyoseph","user":"Hyoseph","date":". 11-18-2013, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/323-hyoseph","name":"Hyoseph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T10:09:58-08:00","id":13469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/12732-covers-and-demonic-form?p=13444#post13444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still I can't quite reconcile the idea that you can damage your Cover while not actually being in that cover. Can someone explain that thought process to me?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect the difference between a regular full transformation and going loud may be part of it, but most evidently even if you haven't got any Cover to lose you still have the chance to pick up Conditions like Flagged and Hunted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T11:09:40-08:00","id":13502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/12732-covers-and-demonic-form?p=13444#post13444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hang on, so you make compromise checks while in Demonic Form which may drop the rating of your cover?</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrugs* It is a mystery...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T11:19:25-08:00","id":13506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyoseph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/12732-covers-and-demonic-form?p=13452#post13452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm with Hawthorn. I don't quite remember whether I saw it, but I seem to remember something about demons shedding their cover briefly into demonic form so that they could do terrible horrible things and not have their cover suffer for it.<br /> <br /> I am interested in how this works as well.<br /> <br /> EDIT - Found it, it's under the Extispicy Exploit:<br /> <br /> &quot;Extispicy works on any living creature of Size 4 or greater. <b>Killing an animal (or a person, for that matter) to read its entrails might constitute a separate compromise if doing so would be grossly out of character for the demon\u2019s Cover. As such, some demons prefer to assume demonic form before gutting the sacrificial creature</b> (the claws often make it easier anyway).&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be part of &quot;acting outside the character of the cover&quot; , which is mentioned as being not &quot;active&quot; when in full demonic form.<br /> Aside from that one part of the cover rolls there is nothing mentioned about the coverr rolls NOT being made on the last asumed cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T11:24:52-08:00","id":13508,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;If a demon encounters a Compromise while in her demonic form, she is not affected by it in a normal way. While in demonic form, the demon is drawing on her past as an angel, while simultaneously overriding her past with her current personality as a demon. Emotions are running high for the demon in this state, and the result of excess stress caused by a Compromise is a raw emotional, if not necessarily human, response. If the demon must roll for a Compromise while in her demonic form, she gains one of the following demonic Conditions instead of a normal Condition as a result of that roll.&quot;<br /> \u2014 &quot;Demonic Conditions,&quot; page 320.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T11:40:13-08:00","id":13518,"title":"","content":"So, given all these quantifiers we can say that -<br /> <br /> - Demons do not make Compromise rolls while in Demonic Form for things that would be &quot;out-of-character&quot; for their Covers. This includes &quot;mortal sins&quot; like murder. <br /> - Demons do still make Compromise rolls while in Demonic Form from other sources e.g. exploit use, multiple use of certain embeds. <br /> - Demons that have to make a Compromise roll (not fail a Compromise roll?) while in Demonic Form gain a Demonic Condition chosen by the player/ST.<br /> <br /> Personally I would add the following -<br /> <br /> - Demons that fail Compromise rolls while in Demonic Form do not loose points from any Cover they posses. They do, however, still take glitches for the failed roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T11:48:11-08:00","id":13525,"title":"","content":"What also is interesting there:<br /> If a demon is in demonic form and looses his last dot of his cover due to comrpomise rolls. Then if he still has another cover he doesn't has to fear loosing another dot of cover until he changes into that cover (as the last cover can't decrease below 0)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T13:18:01-08:00","id":13575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyoseph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/12732-covers-and-demonic-form?p=13452#post13452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm with Hawthorn. I don't quite remember whether I saw it[...]</div> </div> </div> </div>Quoted the very same bit under Extispicy before you did, so I'll wager you saw it in this very thread first. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T14:11:07-08:00","id":13599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/12732-covers-and-demonic-form?p=13518#post13518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, given all these quantifiers we can say that -<br /> <br /> - Demons do not make Compromise rolls while in Demonic Form for things that would be &quot;out-of-character&quot; for their Covers. This includes &quot;mortal sins&quot; like murder.<br /> - Demons do still make Compromise rolls while in Demonic Form from other sources e.g. exploit use, multiple use of certain embeds.<br /> - Demons that have to make a Compromise roll (not fail a Compromise roll?) while in Demonic Form gain a Demonic Condition chosen by the player/ST.<br /> <br /> Personally I would add the following -<br /> <br /> - Demons that fail Compromise rolls while in Demonic Form do not loose points from any Cover they posses. They do, however, still take glitches for the failed roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>(It's <i>failing</i> a Compromise roll, as can be surmised by the &quot;Causing the Condition&quot; block for the writeups of any of the three Demonic Conditions immediately following the portion I quoted.)<br /> <br /> There's also\u2026<br /> <br /> - Demons make Compromise rolls for every scene that they are in Demonic Form, with an increasingly severe penalty on top of the penalty assuming Demonic Form necessitates,* which may either inflict a Condition representing notice by the God-Machine (or fear thereof) or else incur a glitch.**<br /> <br /> *Though I here note that the base penalty listed under &quot;Causes of Compromise&quot; is different from the penalty listed under &quot;Full Transformation&quot; (-3 rather than -2), which should probably be fixed.<br /> ** Presumably the caveat that Conditions are only applied upon resuming Cover only applies to Flagged and Surveilled, being that those Conditions interface with Cover and Hunted and the Demonic Conditions do not.***<br /> *** For similar reasons, it seems redundant to give the Burned the Blown Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-18-2013, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T14:26:13-08:00","id":13616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChairKicker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/12732-covers-and-demonic-form?p=13575#post13575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quoted the very same bit under Extispicy before you did, so I'll wager you saw it in this very thread first. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Could very well be. The price of having internet at work is that I am constantly switching back and forth. Credit for research where credit is due to the Kicker of Chairs <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/323-hyoseph","name":"Hyoseph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T03:17:28-08:00","id":13905,"title":"","content":"No sweat, I'm just amused you took the time to search 600+ pages of text when you could have saved yourself some effort by looking at the previous page. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T06:43:57-08:00","id":13991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/12732-covers-and-demonic-form?p=13599#post13599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(It's <i>failing</i> a Compromise roll, as can be surmised by the &quot;Causing the Condition&quot; block for the writeups of any of the three Demonic Conditions immediately following the portion I quoted.)<br /> <br /> There's also\u2026<br /> <br /> - Demons make Compromise rolls for every scene that they are in Demonic Form, with an increasingly severe penalty on top of the penalty assuming Demonic Form necessitates,* which may either inflict a Condition representing notice by the God-Machine (or fear thereof) or else incur a glitch.**<br /> <br /> *Though I here note that the base penalty listed under &quot;Causes of Compromise&quot; is different from the penalty listed under &quot;Full Transformation&quot; (-3 rather than -2), which should probably be fixed.<br /> ** Presumably the caveat that Conditions are only applied upon resuming Cover only applies to Flagged and Surveilled, being that those Conditions interface with Cover and Hunted and the Demonic Conditions do not.***<br /> *** For similar reasons, it seems redundant to give the Burned the Blown Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>So basically -<br /> <br /> In Cover =<br /> <br /> - A Failed Compromise roll results in a loss of Cover, a Condition being applied or a Glitch.<br /> <br /> Out of Cover/Demonic Form =<br /> <br /> - A Failed Compromise roll results in a Demonic Condition, a Glitch or a Condition. Some of these conditions carry over once the Demon resumes Cover. <br /> - Demons make a Compromise check for every scene they remain in Demonic Form which gets worse over time. <br /> <br /> <br /> So to answer the question at the start of this thread. You can't loose Cover for Compromise checks failed in Demonic Form but you can gain Glitches and Conditions that will carry over back to your Cover and therefore weaken it. <br /> <br /> Cool, glad to clear that up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T10:44:31-08:00","id":14163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/12732-covers-and-demonic-form?p=13991#post13991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So to answer the question at the start of this thread. You can't loose Cover for Compromise checks failed in Demonic Form but you can gain Glitches and Conditions that will carry over back to your Cover and therefore weaken it.<br /> <br /> Cool, glad to clear that up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Further note: gaining a new Cover gets rid of all transient glitches, so the Burned primarily have to worry about outright failure of their Compromise rolls rather than the side-effects of regular success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}